; xhcicmf-amd64.inf - xhcicm.sys as the upper filter of the Thunderbolt and
; USB4 tunnel ports, the 64-bit package's NT-only filter INF (design record
; 21 section 3.3; design record 22 section 3.7; roadmap-usb4.md tasks 39-A.1
; and 40-0.2).
;
; The amd64 counterpart of src\cm\xhcicmf.inf, on the pattern of
; xhcicm-amd64.inf: [Manufacturer] carries the NTamd64,NTamd64.6.0 pair and
; there is no undecorated models or install section, which a 32-bit engine
; would fall back to. The model lines and the install sections are
; xhcicmf.inf's (see that file's header for task 39-0.4's readings; the
; 64-bit guests are not read yet). make-package.ps1 stages this file as
; nt\xhcicmf.inf beside its own copy of xhcicm.sys, its source disk being
; nt\ itself (the driver store refuses a source outside the INF's
; directory; see xhcicmf.inf's header).
;
; scripts\inf-gate\check-cm-inf.ps1 -Filter -Arch amd64 gates this file on
; every build.
;
; ASCII only, CRLF line endings.

[Version]
Signature="$Windows NT$"
Class=System
ClassGUID={4D36E97D-E325-11CE-BFC1-08002BE10318}
Provider=%Provider%
; Must equal src\xhci_version.h.
DriverVer=10/19/2026,3.1.0.0

[Manufacturer]
%Mfg%=CmFilterModels,NTamd64,NTamd64.6.0

[CmFilterModels.NTamd64]
; Record 21 section 3.3's list. The discrete controllers' switch ports;
; 15C0 has been read by this project, every other line is untested.
